 "reachable": true,
 "direction_convention": "Edge P -> Q means 'P reduces to Q' (P <= Q): the reduction transforms an instance of P into an instance of Q. Encoded per reduction .md file by its '# from' (= P, the SOURCE, reduced FROM) and '# to' (= Q, the TARGET, reduced TO) fields; verified against each file's mathematical '# description' (the construction always builds a '# to' instance from a '# from' instance). Out-degree(P) = number of DISTINCT problems P reduces TO = |{Q : an edge P->Q exists}|, i.e. count over P appearing as '# from'. CRITICAL DATA QUIRK: the reduction FILENAME pattern 'from_X_to_Y_<n>.md' is REVERSED relative to the authoritative fields (its X is the '# to' and its Y is the '# from'); the fields, not the filename, were used. Trusting filenames would invert every edge (turning out-degree into in-degree).",
 "counting_rule": "A problem that appears as a vertex in more than one sub-network (classic/approximation/parameterized) is scored by UNION across sub-networks: pool the out-edges of EVERY reduction-network vertex that maps to the atlas row (join via coverage.json 'maps_to' for covered vertices and 'proposed_problem_id' for the 23 uncovered ones -- all 110 vertices resolve), then count DISTINCT TARGET atlas/proposed problem ids. This matches reductions-network-coverage.json's explicit instruction that rn_membership be a SET UNION keyed on 'maps_to', not a 1:1 join. Targets are counted at the canonical (atlas-problem) level, so two reduction-network vertices that map to the same atlas id count as ONE target. Atlas-level SELF-LOOPS are EXCLUDED (a reduction from one encoding of a problem to another encoding of the SAME atlas problem -- e.g. VERTEX COVER -> Vertex Cover with One Fixed Vertex, or directed<->undirected Hamiltonicity -- is not a reduction to a DIFFERENT problem); 19 such self-loops were dropped. Parallel reductions (multiple proof files for the same directed pair) collapse to one edge. Vertices reached via the coverage 'merge' and 'cell' routes ARE included in the union, per the coverage file. Rejected alternatives: (a) SUM across sub-networks would double-count reductions replicated in multiple networks; (b) single chosen network would discard real edges (e.g. clique's 5 parameterized W-hierarchy targets, or vertex-cover's +3 targets from its cubic-graph and approximation vertices).",
 "n_edges": 148,
